{
 "_schema":{
  "purpose":"Scene geometry of the Sekisovskoye twin (spec 4.2). Generated by sekis/geometry.py from params.json and registry.json; regenerate with `python -m sekis.geometry` in team/.",
  "frame":"x east, y up = elevation in metres above sea level, z south; 1 unit = 1 m on every axis. Points are [x, y, z]; plan pairs are [x, z].",
  "numbers":"Coordinates and lengths are rounded to 0.1 m. section_m2, slope_deg, bearing_deg, length_factor and volume_scale keep their own precision.",
  "objects":"One entry per registry thing that has a place in the scene, keyed by thing ID, in registry order. Every entry has kind, primitive, sourced, planned and anchor (label and click point).",
  "scenery":"Drawable items that are not things: surface, old pit, haul roads, yard, streams, pipelines, backfilled blocks. Keyed by a local name; each has primitive and sourced.",
  "sourced":"true: the elevations, cross-section or bearing drawn for the object are published figures. false: at least one of them is an assumption. Plan position is schematic for every object.",
  "planned":"true: the thing is in state planned in the registry (draw dashed). On a link or a decline node it marks a connection below the workings developed at the start. planned_below on an airway is the elevation under which the airway is design only.",
  "primitives":{"box":"center [x,y,z], size [dx,dy,dz], axis-aligned","cylinder":"vertical; base [x,bottom,z], top (elevation), radius, section_m2","frustum":"vertical; base [x,y,z] with radius_base, top (elevation) with radius_top","cone":"base [x,y,z], radius and height at reference_t tonnes","prism":"footprint [[x,z],...] extruded from bottom to top (elevations)","polyline":"points [[x,y,z],...]; width and height of the opening where it is a drive","outline":"footprint [[x,z],...] at elevation y","marker":"a point; the position is anchor"},
  "decline":"points run from the portal to the design bottom, every segment at slope_deg. bottom_elevation is the face at the start (the live value is the twin feature of the same name). nodes are the passing bays: the portal and every 25 m of elevation below it; chainage is metres along points from the portal; type is portal, bay, turn or access (a turn with a level access). Haul distance for travel times is chainage x length_factor.",
  "level":"points is the level drive. links leave the drive: role access (to a decline), crosscut (to a stope), airway (to a shaft or raise), chamber (to a pump station). extent is [x_min, z_min, x_max, z_max] of the level's workings.",
  "mobile":"trucks, loaders and rigs carry mobile true; their box stands on its parking slot. Live positions are the twin features pos_x, pos_y, pos_z."
 },
